    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Can you give me a quick summary of the specific steps a company needs to follow when they receive a formal \"Right to be Forgotten\" request under GDPR? I need to draft an internal memo for our dev team so they know the protocol for deleting user data properly.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A formal \"Right to be Forgotten\" request under GDPR requires your company to meticulously document the entire process, which is a right of the data subject, not just a simple data deletion task. You must first verify the identity of the requester, ensuring they are who they claim to be, before proceeding. If the request is valid, you then need to erase the personal data across all systems, including backups, unless there is a specific legal exemption that allows you to retain it. Finally, you must inform the data subject that the request has been fulfilled, or explain why you are unable to comply.",
